# Prompt Configuration File
# This file contains all parameters needed for prompt execution
# Prompts will automatically read and use these values

## Project Configuration
PROJECT_NAME: My Documentation
PROJECT_DESCRIPTION: Transform knowledge transfer transcripts into structured, searchable documentation

## Agent Configuration
AGENT_NAME: create-docs
AGENT_DESCRIPTION: Transform KT transcripts into structured documentation optimized for both human and AI consumption

## Source Configuration
SOURCE_PATHS:
  - /transcripts/clean/1_Domain_1
  - /transcripts/clean/2_Domain_2

SOURCE_FORMAT: markdown with metadata headers
SOURCE_DESCRIPTION: Knowledge transfer transcripts covering blabla

## Output Configuration
OUTPUT_PATH: /docs
OUTPUT_FORMAT: markdown

## Documentation Conventions
# These values control generated docs entrypoint (SUMMARY.md) and metadata conventions.
# Defaults are provided here so prompts do not require chat-time inputs.
ENTRYPOINT: SUMMARY.md
METADATA_FORMAT: both # yaml-frontmatter | bold-lines | both
CREATE_MODULE_READMES: true
PREFER_SHORT_DOCS: true
SPLIT_THRESHOLD_LINES: 1000
MODULE_README_NAME: README.md

## Domain Configuration
DOMAINS:
  - name: Domain 1
    path: 1_Domain_1
    file_count: 5
    description: My super domain 1
  - name: Domain 2
    path: 2_Domain_2
    file_count: 10
    description: My super domain 2

## Language & Style
LANGUAGE: English
TONE: Professional, technical, clear
AUDIENCE: Technical teams and AI agents

## Processing Configuration
BATCH_SIZE: 2-4 files per batch
PROGRESS_FILE: /temp/create-docs-progress.md
AUTO_BATCH: true

## Quality Requirements
SPECIAL_REQUIREMENTS:
  - Maintain English language throughout
  - Optimize for AI search and discovery
  - Include rich metadata (Topics, Related, Source)
  - Use cross-references with TBD placeholders
  - Maximum 3-4 hierarchy levels

ADDITIONAL_FEATURES:
  - Cross-document references
  - Search optimization keywords
  - Summary index generation
  - Source traceability
  - Progress tracking

## Execution Configuration
EXECUTION_MODE: sequential_batches
VALIDATION_ENABLED: true
AUTO_CROSS_REFERENCE: true
GENERATE_SUMMARY: true

## Model & Tools
TARGET: vscode
TOOLS: [read, edit, search]

## Notes
# To use this configuration:
# 1. Ensure all paths are correct for your workspace
# 2. Call prompts without parameters - they'll read this file automatically
# 3. Update values here instead of passing parameters in chat
# 4. Commit this file to version control for team sharing

## Example Usage
# Instead of:
#   /generic-doc-transformation-agent Create the agent with : [parameters]
#
# Simply call:
#   /generic-doc-transformation-agent Create the agent
#
# The prompt will read all parameters from this file automatically.
